{\b TI Revive} - Total Integration for Access Virus TI on Windows 11\par
\par
TI Revive lets the Access Virus TI work on current Windows without the original Access kernel driver, which Windows 11 blocks. It binds Windows' own Microsoft-signed WinUSB and USB audio drivers to the synthesizer and runs the original Virus TI plug-in and Virus Control Center through a user-mode bridge.\par
\par
{\b Not affiliated} with Access Music Electronics GmbH or Kemper GmbH. "Access", "Virus" and "Virus TI" are trademarks of their owners and are used here only to describe compatibility.\par
\par
TI Revive contains {\b no Access software}. You need your own copy of the Access "Virus TI Software Suite" installer (64-bit .msi). TI Revive installs it for you without its old drivers and without the firmware updater.\par
\par
What TI Revive changes on this computer:\par
- adds a driver package that assigns Windows' WinUSB driver to the Virus TI MIDI interfaces, signed with a certificate created on this computer (its private key is deleted right after signing),\par
- starts a small background process (vtibroker) at logon,\par
- installs the plug-in "Virus TI (TI Revive)" (VST3) and Start menu entries.\par
Uninstalling TI Revive removes all of this again.\par
\par
Provided as is, without warranty. Use at your own risk.\par
